# 14. PREVENT Z-FIGHTING AND RENDERING ARTIFACTS

The previous PM Room experienced overlapping geometry and flickering problems.

Apply those lessons to all new geometry.

Avoid:

- Coplanar overlapping faces.
- Duplicate wall panels.
- Duplicate floors.
- Intersecting decorative surfaces.
- Unnecessary transparent materials.
- Extreme camera depth ranges.
- Duplicate renderer meshes.

Use carefully designed geometry and appropriate material settings.

Only use polygon offset where justified.

Do not globally disable depth testing.

Do not globally enable polygon offset.

Match the established crisp pixel-art rendering style.

Use appropriate texture filtering for pixel-authored textures without damaging materials that need different sampling.

Ensure the exported GLB retains stable geometry independent of preview-only postprocessing.

